cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Decision Wall: ask 200 small yes/no questions at once"
abstract: >-
  An independent, open-source experiment in a way of using fast classifier
  models such as TypeSafe's Jev: break a judgment into many small yes/no
  questions, ask them all in one parallel call, and let code decide what
  counts. Seven question sets of 200 questions render as a live heatmap,
  with Explain, share links and a no-key replay mode. Not affiliated with
  or endorsed by TypeSafe.
authors:
